<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">mining</ansi>

Ore is a trade. Go out with a pick, dig ore, haul it to a forge, then sell it
or smelt it and make something.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Where the ore is ━━━</ansi>

Caves, mountainsides and cliffs carry ore (<ansi fg="command">prospect</ansi> to read them).

  <ansi fg="yellow">Pothole Coulee</ansi>       iron, coal, basalt-iron, copper, some silver;
                       the basalt-iron mine's guarded drifts carry the richest
                       silver and gold
  <ansi fg="yellow">Low Tunnels</ansi>          copper, tin and coal in the goblin warrens
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ironwind Steppe</ansi>      iron and coal in the caves, copper and tin on the cliffs
  <ansi fg="yellow">Eastern Highlands</ansi>    iron, silver, copper, and rarely gold
  <ansi fg="yellow">Cascade Pass Road</ansi>    copper, iron, tin, silver and rarely gold
  <ansi fg="yellow">Stillwater caves</ansi>     lake-iron, copper and tin

Thornwall's drains and cellars hold nothing worth digging.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Ores ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">coal, copper, tin</ansi>    common; any pick
  <ansi fg="yellow">iron</ansi>                 common; any pick
  <ansi fg="yellow">lake-iron, basalt-iron, silver</ansi>   uncommon; an iron pick or better
  <ansi fg="yellow">gold</ansi>                 rare; a steel pick or better, and a strong back

A lucky load may hold a gem: polished stone, gem dust, a raw gem (iron pick)
or, very rarely, a flawless gem (steel pick).

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ From ore to metal ━━━</ansi>

At a forge (blacksmithing): <ansi fg="command">smelt-iron-ore</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">smelt-copper-ore</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">smelt-tin-ore</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">smelt-silver-ore</ansi> (12) and <ansi fg="command">smelt-gold-ore</ansi> (22) make ingots; <ansi fg="command">alloy-bronze</ansi> (6) makes
bronze from copper and tin; <ansi fg="command">steel-ingot</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">crucible-steel</ansi> refine iron further.
At a jeweler's bench (jewelcrafting): <ansi fg="command">draw-copper-wire</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">draw-silver-wire</ansi> (10) and
<ansi fg="command">draw-gold-wire</ansi> (24).

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Metals in gear ━━━</ansi>

Smiths can make a dagger, short sword, buckler or helm in copper, bronze,
silver or gold as well as iron. Against iron:

  <ansi fg="yellow">copper</ansi>   soft and cheap: hits and protects less
  <ansi fg="yellow">bronze</ansi>   nearly iron, a little heavier, handsome
  <ansi fg="yellow">silver</ansi>   soft but quick in the hand; silver armour wards against magic
  <ansi fg="yellow">gold</ansi>     a poor thing to fight with and heavy, but worth a small fortune
           and it makes its wearer more charismatic

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Buying and selling ━━━</ansi>

  Mine Foreman Dagna at the Pothole Coulee Mine Mouth buys ore, ingots and
  coal and sells rough picks. Smith Rusk (Pothole Coulee) and Smith Brindle
  (Stillwater) sell rough picks too. Better picks come only from a smith.

